The last hunk only drops an import that `f32::INFINITY` no longer needs, so the
vendored crate builds without a deprecation warning.

Reproducing
-----------

```bash
curl -L https://crates.io/api/v1/crates/rwhisper/0.4.1/download -o /tmp/rwhisper-0.4.1.crate
tar xf /tmp/rwhisper-0.4.1.crate -C /tmp
diff -ru /tmp/rwhisper-0.4.1/src bridge/vendor/rwhisper/src    # expect exactly the hunks above
```

If a later rwhisper release stops using `TaskType::Unset` here, drop the vendored copy,
restore `rwhisper = "0.4"` in `bridge/Cargo.toml`, and re-run

```bash
cargo run --release --features whisper --example transcribe -- small ru <file.wav>
```

to confirm the patch is no longer needed. That example exists for exactly this check.
